                <pb facs="0687" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 811.001/357: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-30T19:00:00-04:00">September 30, 1919—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3291. From Phillips for Polk. To be deciphered personally by Mr. Polk. Your
                    number 4427 of September 29. Admiral Grayson tells me that the President is
                    troubled by nervous exhaustion which has given rise, to a number of
                    complications, including completely upset digestion. He also is suffering from
                    an attack of asthma and has a great deal of difficulty in sleeping. He will not
                    be able to take up any work whatsoever this week. Grayson believes that by next
                    week he will be able to do a little work. He is much better today than he has
                    been and Grayson is encouraged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
